urs  we see an increase in fluorescence and  it's  important to note that the segmentation  mask corresponds very nicely  in addition you can see not only  the increase in fluorescence you can  also see a qualitative effect  of cell clearing gaps  appearing between the cells within the  co culture  providing additional confidence that  phagocytosis  is occurring  being able to use time-lapse imagery  we can monitor this um phenomena over  the entire time  course of the phagocytosis  on the left-hand side we can here we can  see the time  course of the increase in red  fluorescence area  plotted against time and where you have  apoptotic target cells  where there's been a strong signal for  phagocytosis  you see a large time dependent increase  in fluorescent area  in contrast the non-apoptotic label  target cells where there's a  little or no no stimulus for  phagocytosis  little or no fluorescent increases  observed  and this approach has been taken with a  range of different target cells  and a range of different effector cells  and it's a very robust system  which we feel you can use many many  different cell types  because we can use microtiter plates  this approach  is very amenable to conducting  pharmacological  evaluation and here we've got four  different  inhibitors of  phagocytosis and again we're looking at  the phagocytosis  of apoptosiocats  and we have the highest concentration in  row a  and the lowest concentration in row g  and controls in row h and you can see  um even just looking at the 96 well  plate view  a concentration dependent effect that is  more strongly shown on the right hand  side where we've just taken cytokines in  d  showing that the mean time course from  the we  three replicates and from that we can  derive  the concentration response curve which  enables the determination of an ic50 of  230 nanomolar  so hopefully what i've convinced you so  far is this is a robust  assay of phagocytosis but we want to  demonstrate how this can 