ect  of 24 hours  although these these effects at 24 hours  are outside of the effects that we've  observed phagocytosis  again it begs and second question which  is  is apoptosis being induced by cd47 or  anti-seizure 47 antibody  and so here on the left hand side bar  graph what we have  is the phagocytosis out from the co  culture of cco mceff cem  target cells with j7748.1 mouse  macrophages  or following apoptosis induction with  camtasia you can see a really striking  fatal phagocytosis induction  by contrast though if we look in  monoculture of the  rf cells and look at whether or not  apoptosis is being induced either using  an annexin 5 readout  which looks at ps externalization or a  caspase-37 readout  which looks at the activation of the  caspase  enzyme we can see that there is little  or no activity  of the anti-cd47 antibody by contrast to  the camtasia which we know  will induce apoptosis this is  really strong evidence that that  anti-cd47  induced phagocytosis is not acting  through an apoptosis induction  so to try to wrap everything up into a  simple summary  hopefully i've demonstrated that  real-time lifestyle analysis  coupled with a novel reagent  enables direct cell measurements  of phagocytosis and adds true  valuable biological insight and enhanced  productivity  which is in contrast with some of the  common cell-based assay methods  where fixing and or lifting is required  and there's really a lack of temporal  resolution or verification by  visualization and importantly  this approach is very amenable  to the characterization of anti-cd47  antibodies  which promote phagocytosis and really  certainly commensurate with the descr  modulators and potentially other  modulators of phagocytosis by  macrophages  and this whole approach can be  complemented  by using other real-time  applications such as proliferation and  apoptosis  to either confirm or deny other  mechanisms

